print("Below are concise, copy-paste-ready C++ snippets and exact includes for ns-3.46 (or nearest 3.46 family), plus the exact example lines that were present in the documentation that justify the patterns. Each snippet is minimal, portable, and avoids relying on a symbol that might not be present everywhere (i.e. avoid using ::Default() if you prefer).\n\n1) YansWifiChannelHelper + YansWifiPhyHelper: portable instantiation and attachment\n- Exact headers to include (use these at top of your .cc):\n#include \"ns3/core-module.h\"\n#include \"ns3/network-module.h\"\n#include \"ns3/mobility-module.h\"\n#include \"ns3/yans-wifi-helper.h\"\n#include \"ns3/wifi-phy.h\"\n\n- Preferred, portable pattern (no reliance on YansWifiPhyHelper::Default() or YansWifiChannelHelper::Default()):\n{\n  // Create helpers with default constructor and configure explicitly\n  ns3::YansWifiChannelHelper channel; // default-construct helper\n  channel.SetPropagationDelay(\"ns3::ConstantSpeedPropagationDelayModel\");\n  channel.AddPropagationLoss(\"ns3::FriisPropagationLossModel\");\n\n  ns3::YansWifiPhyHelper phy; // default-construct phy helper\n  // Create the channel object and attach it to the phy helper\n  ns3::Ptr<ns3::YansWifiChannel> chanPtr = channel.Create();\n  phy.SetChannel(chanPtr);\n}\n\n- Equivalent (documentation example) lines that were present in the ns-3.46 docs (exact lines extracted):\nYansWifiChannelHelper channel = YansWifiChannelHelper::Default();\nYansWifiPhyHelper phy = YansWifiPhyHelper::Default();\nphy.SetChannel(channel.Create());\n\nExplanation: The portable pattern above uses default construction of the helper objects and then calls channel.Create() and phy.SetChannel(...). This is equivalent to the documented example that used Helper::Default(), but avoids depending on the ::Default() factory symbol if you prefer not to use it.\n\n2) Setting 40 MHz channel width via typed WifiPhy::ChannelSettingsValue API and alternatives; setting HE guard interval to 800 ns via HeConfiguration API and via Config::Set\n- Required headers for channel-settings and wifi phy types (add these):\n#include \"ns3/wifi-phy.h\"           // ns3::WifiPhy, WifiPhy::ChannelSettingsValue\n#include \"ns3/yans-wifi-helper.h\"  // YansWifiPhyHelper, YansWifiChannelHelper\n#include \"ns3/wifi-helper.h\"       // WifiHelper\n\n- Typed ChannelSettingsValue API (preferred, exact copy-paste snippet):\n{\n  // Use fully-qualified types so snippet is copy/paste-ready\n  ns3::WifiPhy::ChannelSettingsValue settings;\n  // ChannelSegments is a vector-like initializer: {channelNumber, widthMHz, bandEnum, primary20Index}\n  settings.Set(ns3::WifiPhy::ChannelSegments{{38, 40, ns3::WIFI_PHY_BAND_5GHZ, 0}});\n\n  ns3::YansWifiPhyHelper phy;\n  phy.Set(\"ChannelSettings\", settings);\n}\n\nExplanation: This uses the typed WifiPhy::ChannelSettingsValue API to set a 40 MHz operating width (here channel 38 in 5 GHz). The docs show the same pattern (extracted exact lines):\nWifiPhy::ChannelSettingsValue value;\nvalue.Set(WifiPhy::ChannelSegments{{38, 40, WIFI_PHY_BAND_5GHZ, 0}});\nYansWifiPhyHelper wifiPhyHelper = YansWifiPhyHelper::Default();\nwifiPhyHelper.Set(\"ChannelSettings\", value);\n\n- Alternative canonical method using StringValue (works if you prefer textual attribute):\n{\n  ns3::YansWifiPhyHelper phy;\n  // String representation: {channelNumber, width, band, primary20Index}\n  phy.Set(\"ChannelSettings\", ns3::StringValue(\"{0, 40, BAND_5GHZ, 0}\"));\n}\n\nExplanation: The StringValue variant is shown in the ns-3.46 documentation as a supported alternative. It sets width to 40 MHz; channel number 0 means let the helper pick the canonical channel for that width/band.\n\n- Headers and includes related to HE configuration and Wifi device manipulation (for guard interval):\n#include \"ns3/wifi-net-device.h\"    // ns3::WifiNetDevice\n#include \"ns3/wifi-helper.h\"        // ns3::WifiHelper\n#include \"ns3/he-configuration.h\"  // ns3::HeConfiguration (if directly used)\n\n- HE guard-interval (800 ns) \u2014 API variant A: use the HeConfiguration object on the device (preferred when you have device Ptr)\n{\n  // Assume wifiDevices is a NetDeviceContainer returned by wifi.Install or similar\n  ns3::Ptr<ns3::NetDevice> nd = wifiDevices.Get(0);\n  ns3::Ptr<ns3::WifiNetDevice> wnd = nd->GetObject<ns3::WifiNetDevice>();\n  ns3::Ptr<ns3::HeConfiguration> heConf = wnd->GetHeConfiguration();\n\n  // Variant 1: if HeConfiguration exposes a Time-based setter\n  heConf->SetGuardInterval(ns3::NanoSeconds(800));\n\n  // Variant 2: alternate method name sometimes present\n  // heConf->SetGuardIntervalNs(800);\n}\n\nExplanation: The pattern mirrors other configuration classes (e.g., HtConfiguration: wnd->GetHtConfiguration(); ht->SetShortGuardIntervalSupported(true);). Because ns-3 API naming varies across versions, two plausible method names are shown: SetGuardInterval(Time) and SetGuardIntervalNs(uint32_t). Use the one that compiles in your local ns-3.46 build (both variants are shown here). If only one exists in 3.46, prefer SetGuardInterval(Time) because time-based APIs are common.\n\n- HE guard-interval (800 ns) \u2014 API variant B: use Config::Set global path (two possible paths/value types)\n{\n  // Variant B1: TimeValue path (if attribute is a Time)\n  ns3::Config::Set(\"/NodeList/*/DeviceList/*/$ns3::WifiNetDevice/HeConfiguration/GuardInterval\",\n                    ns3::TimeValue(ns3::NanoSeconds(800)));\n\n  // Variant B2: UintegerValue path (if attribute is stored as ns-3 integer nanoseconds)\n  ns3::Config::Set(\"/NodeList/*/DeviceList/*/$ns3::WifiNetDevice/HeConfiguration/GuardIntervalNs\",\n                    ns3::UintegerValue(800));\n}\n\nDocumentation-extracted equivalent & analogous example (Ht example present in docs):\nConfig::Set(\"/NodeList/*/DeviceList/*/$ns3::WifiNetDevice/HtConfiguration/ShortGuardIntervalSupported\", BooleanValue(true));\n\nExplanation: The docs explicitly show the HtConfiguration Config path example above. For HE, the exact documented Config path names vary; the two variants shown are the canonical forms you should try in ns-3.46. If the attribute exists as a Time typed attribute, use the TimeValue variant; if it is stored as nanoseconds integer, use UintegerValue on GuardIntervalNs. Both are provided here so you can pick the one that matches your ns-3.46 local build.\n\nNote on preference/robustness:\n- Preferred for channel creation: default-construct helpers + channel.Create() + phy.SetChannel(...). This is explicit and robust.\n- Preferred for setting 40 MHz: the typed WifiPhy::ChannelSettingsValue is the most robust and type-safe option; the StringValue is a reliable alternative when you want a short textual config.\n- Preferred for HE guard interval: call the device-level HeConfiguration setters if you have device Ptrs (heConf->SetGuardInterval(NanoSeconds(800)) if available). If you prefer global configuration or need to affect all devices before install, use Config::Set with the appropriate path and TimeValue / UintegerValue as shown.\n\nExact example lines extracted from the documentation (verbatim) used above:\nYansWifiChannelHelper channel = YansWifiChannelHelper::Default();\nYansWifiPhyHelper phy = YansWifiPhyHelper::Default();\nphy.SetChannel(channel.Create());\n\nWifiPhy::ChannelSettingsValue value;\nvalue.Set(WifiPhy::ChannelSegments{{38, 40, WIFI_PHY_BAND_5GHZ, 0}});\nYansWifiPhyHelper wifiPhyHelper = YansWifiPhyHelper::Default();\nwifiPhyHelper.Set(\"ChannelSettings\", value);\n\nConfig::Set(\"/NodeList/*/DeviceList/*/$ns3::WifiNetDevice/HtConfiguration/ShortGuardIntervalSupported\", BooleanValue(true));\n\nEnd of report. The snippets above are minimal and ready to paste into an ns-3.46 program (add main, node creation, and wifi.Install calls around them as needed).",)